{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04AB", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bcf670a6e7b08c7a83d1e6786dd742906e6896877480d6a3e04d714d54b733e3", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nEspecially when taking quotients by group actions the following definition\nis useful.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3d03e1ca6676db5331965b59de8940ac5878ea44369ecba0d1176767c9a852fb", "unit_id": "tag:04AB:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04AB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$j : R \\to U \\times_B U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\phi : U \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$B$", "MATH_0007": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0008": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0009": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0010": "$X$", "MATH_0011": "$R$", "MATH_0012": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{item-intersect-invariant-closed}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-good}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9aad6a16aad4b13da41ef9d6543082bfd824a917a0959c44e6db172aac545833", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a101d81513b524b9d7ab1479142cea98f95d6b507889a0da06bfbd677fe6c0b3", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme and <MATH_0002> an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a pre-relation.\nA morphism <MATH_0005> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0006>\nis called a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>good quotient<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0007> is invariant,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0008> is affine,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0009> is surjective,\n<STRUCT_0005> condition (<REF_0001>) holds universally, and\n<STRUCT_0006> the functions on <MATH_0010> are the <MATH_0011>-invariant functions on <MATH_0012>.\n<STRUCT_0007>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9f02af426c6d4a4f5c39a86a3dfb224302f703dcf70eea5c6656c26df8c7e74b", "unit_id": "tag:04AC:statement"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04AB", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\cite{seshadri_quotients}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{item-intersect-invariant-closed}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:674907e49a5254ce2c5013b0e3bc79911de38d81ede5e892400783af296184b3", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn <REF_0001> Seshadri gives almost the same definition,\nexcept that instead of (4) he simply requires the condition\n(<REF_0002>) to hold -- he does not require\nit to hold universally.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:279da2dc866e9ca5ef857eb39be3b80c3a7e9427703ee5e9645501667d629b9e", "unit_id": "tag:04AB:prose-0002"}
